%% seq_05b_org_update_member_role.mmd
%% Updated 2026-07-17 (verified).
%% Reader intent: Understand how an org admin changes an existing member's authority.
%% Key boundary: Role-change sequence only; invite/add/remove paths are separate.
%% Current caveat: Role validation compares actor and target authority, so the main risk sits in permission hierarchy rather than raw update mechanics.

sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Admin as Org Owner/Admin
    participant B as Browser
    participant C as Controller
    participant Cmd as UpdateMemberRoleCommand
    participant Repo as OrganizationUserRepository
    participant DB as PostgreSQL
    participant Audit as auditPublicApi

    Admin->>B: Select new role
    B->>C: Submit role change
    C->>Cmd: execute(dto)
    Cmd->>Repo: getMemberRoleName(actor)
    Repo->>DB: SELECT actor role
    DB-->>Repo: Actor role
    Cmd->>Repo: getMemberRoleName(target)
    Repo->>DB: SELECT target role
    DB-->>Repo: Target role
    Cmd->>Cmd: Enforce org permission policy

    alt Policy denies change
        Cmd-->>C: Forbidden / conflict error
        C-->>B: Show error
    else Change allowed
        Cmd->>Repo: updateRole(orgId, userId, newRole)
        Repo->>DB: UPDATE organization_users
        Cmd->>Audit: write role-change audit log
        Audit->>DB: INSERT audit_events + audit_event_scopes
        Cmd-->>C: Success
        C-->>B: Redirect with success flash
    end
